<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brazzaville</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brazzaville is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-river">Congo River</a>, now the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-the-congo">Republic of the Congo</a>. It was founded in the 1880s and became the headquarters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-equatorial-africa">French Equatorial Africa</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> administered its West and Equatorial African federations from Dakar and Brazzaville respectively.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brazzaville.jpg" alt="Brazzaville" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Africany · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Les_lieux_de_Brazzaville_03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
